<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
<!--
  ⚠️ INVESTIGATION / WORKAROUND ONLY — NOT PR-READY. ⚠️
  This sample deliberately bypasses "Sdk=MSTest.Sdk" for internal research/verification purposes
  only (see the blog-post publication gate this sample supports). It is NOT the form we intend to
  ship or recommend to readers, and this commit should not be proposed as a PR until the revert
  checklist below is satisfied.

  Revert checklist (do this once a public MSTest.Sdk release ships the fixed AOT wiring —
  see files/source-generation-sdk-gap.md for the tracking issue and acceptance criteria):
    [ ] Switch back to <Project Sdk="MSTest.Sdk"> (the commented-out block at the bottom of this
        file shows the exact target shape).
    [ ] Remove the explicit MSTest.SourceGeneration / MSTest.TestAdapter / MSTest.TestFramework
        PackageReferences below — MSTest.Sdk's PublishAot=true wiring should add them.
    [ ] Remove the MSTestSourceGenerationVersion workaround property (and its comment) from
        ../Directory.Build.props once MSTestAOTVersion/MSTestEngineVersion resolve the same
        reflection-free generator through the SDK.
    [ ] Re-verify: dotnet build (managed) AND a real `dotnet publish -r <rid> -p:PublishAot=true`
        run of the resulting native binary, not just the managed test host.
    [ ] Remove this banner and the "workaround" prose from the .csproj comments once the above is
        confirmed; only then is this sample change appropriate to open as a PR.
-->
<!--
This sample intentionally does NOT use "Sdk=MSTest.Sdk". As of MSTest.Sdk 4.3.3 (see ../global.json),
MSTest.Sdk's PublishAot=true convenience wiring still resolves the deprecated, discontinued MSTest.Engine
package and the old Engine-era MSTest.SourceGeneration build (MSTestEngineVersion in Directory.Build.props) -
NOT the current reflection-free source generator described in docs/source-generator/design.md. Until a
newer MSTest.Sdk decouples its Native AOT wiring from MSTest.Engine, referencing MSTest.SourceGeneration
directly (as below) is how to get today's actual reflection-free behavior: test classes/methods/attributes
are materialized at compile time and registered with the MSTest adapter via ReflectionMetadataHook.Register,
with no reflection scan and no separate test-framework engine.
-->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>

    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
    <EnableMSTestRunner>true</EnableMSTestRunner>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeCoverage.MSBuild" Version="$(CodeCoverageVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.CodeCoverage" Version="$(CodeCoverageVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.TrxReport" Version="$(TestingPlatformVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Testing.Platform.MSBuild" Version="$(TestingPlatformVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.Analyzers" Version="$(MSTestVersion)" />
    <!-- $(MSTestSourceGenerationVersion), not $(MSTestAOTVersion): see the comment above and in Directory.Build.props. -->
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.SourceGeneration" Version="$(MSTestSourceGenerationVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestAdapter" Version="$(MSTestVersion)" />
    <PackageReference Include="MSTest.TestFramework" Version="$(MSTestVersion)" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Microsoft.VisualStudio.TestTools.UnitTesting" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>

<!--
Below is the equivalent project configuration using MSTest.Sdk. It is simpler, but as explained above,
currently (MSTest.Sdk 4.3.3) produces the deprecated Engine-era generator rather than the reflection-free
one this sample is demonstrating. Once MSTest.Sdk ships an update that tracks MSTest.SourceGeneration
independently of MSTest.Engine, this will become the recommended, simplest way to opt in.

<Project Sdk="MSTest.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>

    ' When MSTest Sdk detects PublishAot=true, it references the required packages to ensure Native AOT support. '
    <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
-->
